# Written for this pack by BurN-30 (GPL-3.0). From the Zul'Farrak steps of 23-tanaris.guide (sources:
# Polestar's Dungeons codex, data-v2026.11.1, and Wowhead Forever; Velratha's courtyard and the
# pool: Warcraft Tavern's Forever Zul'Farrak guide read on 11/11/2026, itself from Classic; the
# pyramid event from the original game). Not played in game yet.
#
# Self-contained chapter for Polestar's own route: the Groupe Alliance module offers it once Tran'rek
# (2864) is handed in at Gadgetzan, the first stop of forever/alliance/40-50/04-tanaris (about 46),
# and opens it in a tab of its own: the three Gadgetzan quests, the ride to the walled city, the run,
# the rewards at Gadgetzan. Polestar's guide keeps its place and comes back at the end.
#
# Compared with Polestar 0.4.2.2's own Zul'Farrak (data/dungeon-runs.json, run "Zul'Farrak" for the
# Alliance, written into 40-50/04-tanaris as `when dungeon` steps that 0.4.2.2 reads as skipped; and
# its Dungeons codex page "zulfarrak", Polestar_Codex, GPL-3.0):
# - the same three quests and the same place to take them: Scarab Shells (2865, after Tran'rek 2864,
#   which the route hands in), Troll Temper (3042), Divino-matic Rod (2768); Polestar runs the
#   dungeon later in its guide, from the pool by Sandsorrow Watch, about 400 yards from the gate, and
#   hands them in at its next Gadgetzan stop: this chapter goes at once, from Gadgetzan;
# - its "leftOut" list and this chapter agree: Gahz'rilla (2770, a second run, greffe/zul-farrak-2),
#   The Prophecy of Mosh'aru (3527, after Screecher Spirits, not on the route), Nekrum's Medallion
#   (2991, open only at 50-51 on the route), Tiara of the Deep (2846, Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh, off
#   the route), the OOX-17/TN beacon;
# - on its page and not here either: The Witch Doctor's Head (96770, Archmage Lan'dalock in the Alterac
#   Mountains, off the route at this level).
guide groupe-alliance/greffe/zul-farrak
title Dungeon · Zul'Farrak (45-50)
folder Group Alliance
category Dungeons
faction Alliance
levels 45-50
zone Tanaris

step Zul'Farrak: Gadgetzan
  zone Tanaris
  tip Zul'Farrak: a troll city in the north-west of Tanaris, levels 44 to 54, best at 45 or more with a full group. Three quests from Gadgetzan, all done inside: Tran'rek on the north side of town, Trenton Lighthammer and Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle by the water tower.
  note Keep 3 free quest log slots.
  accept 2865                         -- Tran'rek: Scarab Shells
  accept 3042                         -- Trenton Lighthammer: Troll Temper
  accept 2768                         -- Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle: Divino-matic Rod

step Zul'Farrak
  zone Tanaris
  tip Ride north-west from Gadgetzan to the walled city, at the edge of the dunes. Inside, every troll can drop Troll Temper; the scarabs by the graveyard of Theka the Martyr drop the shells.
  tip The pyramid event: free Sergeant Bly and his crew from the cage at the top of the stairs, then hold the stairs against the troll waves. Once the trolls are dead, Bly turns on you: he drops the Divino-matic Rod.
  note Group of 5: share each quest (quest log, Share) before going in. Chief Ukorz Sandscalp, the last boss, waits behind the door Weegli blows open after the pyramid event.
  note Hydromancer Velratha holds the courtyard of the great pool, round the corner from the entrance: whoever took Tabetha's Tiara of the Deep in Dustwallow Marsh finds the tiara on her. A rare OOX-17/TN Distress Beacon can drop here, as from most of the creatures of Tanaris: the guide does not follow it.
  goto 38.7,20.1 "Zul'Farrak"
  collect 9238 x5 quest 2865          -- Uncracked Scarab Shell
  collect 9523 x20 quest 3042         -- Troll Temper
  collect 8548 quest 2768             -- Divino-matic Rod: Sergeant Bly

step Gadgetzan: Zul'Farrak rewards
  zone Tanaris
  tip Last stop of the chapter: the route's own guide comes back once these are handed in.
  turnin 2865                         -- Tran'rek
  turnin 3042                         -- Trenton Lighthammer
  turnin 2768                         -- Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle
